.TH EMAIL\-IMPORT\-RULES 1 "" "email-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
email\-import\-rules \- import Thunderbird message filters into email-cli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B email\-import\-rules
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Converts Thunderbird
.I msgFilterRules.dat
files into the
.I rules.ini
format used by
.BR email\-cli (1).
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-account ,
every configured account is processed and each Thunderbird filter is matched
to the account whose IMAP server it belongs to, using the profile's
.IR prefs.js .
.PP
Filter elements that have no equivalent are reported on standard error as
.B [warn]
lines and skipped; the rest of the rule is still converted. Run with
.B \-\-dry\-run
first to see exactly what would be written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-thunderbird\-path " dir"
Thunderbird profile directory. Auto\-detected from
.I ~/.thunderbird
when omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-account " email"
Import for this account only.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " path"
Write to this file instead of the account's
.IR rules.ini .
Requires
.BR \-\-account .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the converted rules without saving.
.TP
.B \-\-version ", " \-\-help ", " \-h
Version and help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/email\-cli/accounts/<email>/rules.ini
Destination rule file. Apply the rules with
.BR "email\-sync \-\-apply\-rules" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non\-zero on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR email\-cli (1),
.BR email\-sync (1)
